        "Create a compact comparison sheet with four columns: expected feature, visible evidence, confidence and action. A row might say ‘navy option selected,’ ‘dark blue fabric appears in three frames,’ ‘medium confidence because lighting is warm,’ and ‘request neutral-light view if exact shade matters.’ Another row might record ‘size 42 selected,’ ‘label shows 42 clearly,’ ‘high confidence,’ and ‘no follow-up.’ This structure separates identity checks from aesthetic judgment and reveals exactly which missing view would change the decision."
