        "For multi-piece products, quantity must be proved by a frame that shows all expected parts or by separate images that can be matched without duplication. A box in the background does not prove its contents. Likewise, a closed pocket does not prove that an accessory is inside. Build the check around the seller’s included-parts description and mark every unseen component as unverified. This is especially important when one listing contains several configurations; the correct main item can arrive with the wrong accessory set."
